      'The three middlewares are on by default on the operator\'s personal agent as of the README\'s 2026.21.1 note, and each is described as failing safe where the other two cannot.',
      'The quickstart requires Python 3.12+ and uv, plus `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY` or `MINIMAX_API_KEY` to run the examples.',
      '`bindu deploy agent.py --runtime=boxd` ships a script to a microVM and prints an HTTPS URL with no Dockerfile; the README lists an Agent Swarm example and a Premium Advisor example where the caller pays USDC before anything runs.',
      'Callers POST to `http://localhost:3773/` with curl, then poll `tasks/get` with the same `taskId` until the state reaches `completed`.',
